# Task 167-004 Execution Plan — T4 Memory.db + Data Integrity Audit

## Objective
READ-ONLY forensic audit of `.brain/memory.db` SQLite database. Produce findings in `.audit/sprint-167/T4-memory-integrity.md` (≥300 lines) + a GO/NO_GO predicate script `.audit/sprint-167/T4-predicate.sh`.

## Scope Reminder
- NO source/doc/db mutation. `.brain/memory.db` opened READ-ONLY (`sqlite3 -readonly` or `file:?mode=ro`).
- Write target: `.audit/sprint-167/` only.

## Audit Plan (3 sub-stages mapped to spec)

### 4.1 Entry Consistency
- Total entry count vs ~215 claim
- Sprint_id ↔ sprint_num parity (regex extract num from `sprint-NNN`)
- Type/status enumeration + cardinality
- decay_exempt distribution (identity / mandatory ADRs should be exempt)
- Detect insufficient body entries (e.g. mem-sprint-165 ~30 bytes)
- Detect orphan sprint_id refs (sprint_num exists but no sprint log file)

### 4.2 FTS5 + Relations Integrity
- FTS5 rowid parity with entries table (entries_fts trigger sync)
- Dual-layer normalize: TR/EN/DE sample queries (3+ tests)
- Relations: broken to_id / from_id (orphan FK)
- Relation type enumeration
- entry_history coverage analysis

### 4.3 Schema, Backup, Bug Z3
- Schema version drift (schema_version table vs implementation expectation `version=1`)
- Backup pattern inventory (.bak-* files + gitignore confirmation)
- Bug Z3 impact analysis — memory rebuild destructive behavior
- Restore TEST: forbidden (audit only)

## Files To Write
1. `.audit/sprint-167/T4-memory-integrity.md` (≥300 lines, ≥3 FTS5 mentions, ≥1 Bug Z3 mention)
2. `.audit/sprint-167/T4-predicate.sh` (GO/NO_GO predicate runner)

## Verify Loop
No source code changes → tsc/vitest do not apply. Predicate script self-verifies.

## Output Quality Gates
- ≥300 lines markdown
- ≥6 sections
- 4-field finding format where applicable (severity / suggested_fix / sprint_slot / effort_estimate)
- predicate.sh exits 0 PASS / non-zero FAIL with explicit reason
